Conjunction License

Copyright (c) 2026 MaximdeWinter. All rights reserved, except for what this license allows.

"Conjunction" means the app, its source code, the Conjunction Runtime and every build of them.


You may:

1. Download, install and use Conjunction, for free.
2. Read the source code, build it and change it for your own use.
3. Share the quests, places, mods and content packs you make with Conjunction. The scripts and files
   Conjunction adds to them (for example the quest's script functions and the pack card) may go with them.
4. Write plug-ins for Conjunction and share them, as long as they hold no code of Conjunction.
5. Link to Conjunction's official pages (Nexus Mods and GitHub).


You may not:

1. Upload or share Conjunction, a changed version of it or a build of it (on mod sites, file hosts, in other
   repositories or in a pack with other files). The official pages are the only places to download it.
2. Sell Conjunction or a changed version of it, or charge for access to it.
3. Hand out Conjunction or a changed version of it as your own work.

A fork on GitHub (GitHub's terms allow it) is for your own changes. It may not publish builds or releases.


What you make with Conjunction

Everything you make with Conjunction (quests, places, mods, content packs, plug-ins, exports) is the property of its
creator. The creator decides what happens with it and is responsible for its content. MaximdeWinter takes no
responsibility for content made with Conjunction.

A credit is welcome ("Made with Conjunction" with a link to its page). It is not required.


Third-party parts

Conjunction contains software of other authors (Python, Qt for Python, PyYAML, Pillow, cryptography, lz4 and more).
These parts stay under their own licenses, listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and the licenses folder. Where one of them gives you more rights (for example to replace the Qt libraries), those
rights apply to that part.


